ELD Ubuntu/PPA packaging
========================

This is a native source package built from the LLVM 21-compatible ELD release
line. Ubuntu's llvm-21-dev package is used directly; LLVM is not bundled.

The ubuntu_packaging branch must always contain exactly one commit on top of
native-llvm21. Keep packaging edits in that commit:

  git switch ubuntu_packaging
  git add <changed-files>
  git commit --amend --no-edit
  git push --force-with-lease rustedsword ubuntu_packaging

When native-llvm21 advances, rebase the single packaging commit onto it, then
amend and force-push with lease. publish.sh verifies the branch, ancestry,
commit count, and clean-tree invariant before a normal upload.

Launchpad versions are immutable. Before each new upload, add a changelog entry
with a unique version (increment +gxrN), then amend the existing packaging
commit. The changelog targets resolute with a ~26.04.N suffix; publish.sh
reuses that entry for every other supported series with its own ~XX.XX.N
suffix (stonking: ~26.10.N).

Publishing runs in an Ubuntu 26.04 Podman container. On the signing host, use
./publish.sh --no-upload for a signed validation build and ./publish.sh to sign
and upload resolute and stonking builds to ppa:lightofmysoul/gxr;
--series CODENAME limits a run to one series. Without a private key, use
./publish.sh --unsigned; unsigned artifacts cannot be uploaded.
